#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "auto.provisioning"

Feature:  Auto Provisioning Ticket
	Testing to assure auto provisioning tickets work properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | usr.provisioning1                       |
	| Email Address | usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | USR                                     |
	| Last Name     | Provisioning1                           |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Provis - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Propar - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Propar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Provis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Vispro - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| PROPAR       |
	| VISPROPROVIS |
	| VISPRO       |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| PROPAR       |
	| VISPROPROVIS |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Propar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Provis - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Propar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Provis - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Create project for US Support Region and view ticket
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Testing the ability to view an autoprovisioning ticket

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I publish a partner account RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Propar - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | abcdefgh1234567890                         |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Professional Services (Technical/Web/IT)   |
	| Owner Email Address                    | usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken    |
	| Owner First Name                       | USR                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Provisioning1                              |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Name                           | Service Partnership                        |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | 000000a1b2c3d4e5f6e7f                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	And I publish a project RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Vispro - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken    |
	| Contact First Name                     | USR                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Provisioning1                              |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Engineering                                |
	| Owner Email Address                    | usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken    |
	| Owner First Name                       | USR                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Provisioning1                              |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Partner Dossiera Key                   | abcdefgh1234567890                         |
	| Partner Name                           | Propar - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Partner Support Level                  | Platinum                                   |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Provis - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Provis"
	And I click on the account with the name "Provis - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the Sync To Zendesk button on the account page
	Then the support organization with the code "VISPROPROVIS" should be part of the support site
	And I wait for "3" minutes
	Then the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Provis - ${staticProjectName}" should be synced to zendesk
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Provis - ${staticProjectName}" should have the support region "provisioning_united_states"
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Provis - ${staticProjectName}" should have the primary address country "United States"
	When I go to the OSB admin main page
	Then I should be able to view a project with the name "Provis - ${staticProjectName}" and following values
	| Koroneiki Account Key | Obtain from project name      |
	| Project Name          | Provis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code                  | VISPROPROVIS                  |
	| Partner               | Propar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Addresses             | 456 Fake Street               |
	| Addresses             | United States                 |
	| Addresses             | California                    |
	| Addresses             | Diamond Bar                   |
	| Addresses             | 91765                         |
	| Addresses             | Primary                       |
	| Tier                  | T4                            |
	| Language              | English                       |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki account with the name "Provis - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Language    | English       | |
	| Region      | United States | |
	| Data Region | United States | |
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Provis - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" with the following values
	| Quantity | 1        | |
	| Status   | Approved | |
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Provis - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Platinum Subscription" with the following values
	| Quantity | 1        | |
	| Status   | Approved | |
	And the contact with the email address "usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Provis - ${staticProjectName}" should have the contact role "Support User"
	And the contact with the email address "usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Provis - ${staticProjectName}" should have the contact role "Liferay Sales"
	And the contact with the email address "usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Provis - ${staticProjectName}" should have the contact role "Secondary Contact"

Scenario: Create project for Australia Support Region and view ticket
	Testing the ability to create a project for the Australia support region using RabbitMQ auto provisioning

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I publish a partner account RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Propar - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | abcdefgh1234567890                         |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Professional Services (Technical/Web/IT)   |
	| Owner Email Address                    | usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken    |
	| Owner First Name                       | USR                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Provisioning1                              |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Name                           | Service Partnership                        |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | 000000a1b2c3d4e5f6e7f                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	And I publish a project RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Vispro - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Sydney                                     |
	| Address Country                        | Australia                                  |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 2000                                       |
	| Address Region                         | New South Wales                            |
	| Address Street                         | 227 Elizabeth Street                       |
	| Contact Email Address                  | usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken    |
	| Contact First Name                     | USR                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Provisioning1                              |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Engineering                                |
	| Owner Email Address                    | usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken    |
	| Owner First Name                       | USR                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Provisioning1                              |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Partner Dossiera Key                   | abcdefgh1234567890                         |
	| Partner Name                           | Propar - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Partner Support Level                  | Platinum                                   |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Provis - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay Australia                          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | Australia                                  |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Provis"
	And I click on the account with the name "Provis - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the Sync To Zendesk button on the account page
	Then the support organization with the code "VISPROPROVIS" should be part of the support site
	And I wait for "3" minutes
	Then the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Provis - ${staticProjectName}" should be synced to zendesk
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Provis - ${staticProjectName}" should have the support region "provisioning_australia"
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for Provis - ${staticProjectName}" should have the primary address country "Australia"
	When I go to the OSB admin main page
	Then I should be able to view a project with the name "Provis - ${staticProjectName}" and following values
	| Koroneiki Account Key | Obtain from project name      |
	| Project Name          | Provis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code                  | VISPROPROVIS                  |
	| Partner               | Propar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Addresses             | 227 Elizabeth Street          |
	| Addresses             | Australia                     |
	| Addresses             | New South Wales               |
	| Addresses             | Sydney                        |
	| Addresses             | 2000                          |
	| Addresses             | Primary                       |
	| Tier                  | T4                            |
	| Language              | English                       |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki account with the name "Provis - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Language    | English   | |
	| Region      | Australia | |
	| Data Region | Japan     | |
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Provis - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" with the following values
	| Quantity | 1        | |
	| Status   | Approved | |
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Provis - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Platinum Subscription" with the following values
	| Quantity | 1        | |
	| Status   | Approved | |
	And the contact with the email address "usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Provis - ${staticProjectName}" should have the contact role "Support User"
	And the contact with the email address "usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Provis - ${staticProjectName}" should have the contact role "Liferay Sales"
	And the contact with the email address "usr.provisioning1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Provis - ${staticProjectName}" should have the contact role "Secondary Contact"

